\title{A guard that keeps an order's limit from crossing the book}
\description{
The \code{post_only} guard of a plan: a limit checked against the book before it is sent or moved, so that it rests rather than trades.

A buy is passive below the best offer and a sell above the best bid. A limit that would cross is refused with \code{on_crossing} \code{refuse}, which ends the order, or moved back to its own side's touch with \code{rest}; a move of a resting order that would cross is skipped with \code{refuse} and held at the own touch with \code{rest}. Indian exchanges have no post-only flag, so the book can still move while the order is in flight. It goes in \code{OrderPart$new(guard = ...)}. UBI refuses it on a stop with \code{post_only_needs_limit}, and with pricing that means to trade at once, \code{MarketablePricing}, \code{ChasePricing}, a \code{PegPricing} to the \code{opposite_touch} or a market order, with \code{post_only_crosses}.
}
